    "text": {
     "en": "A bank keeps our savings safe and pays interest on them. It also lends money to people for homes, farms and business and charges interest on loans.\nThe money we put in is a deposit. Interest is the extra amount paid for using money. If we deposit 1,000 rupees at 5 percent a year we earn 50 rupees in a year.\nThe Reserve Bank of India regulates banks. We should keep passwords and PINs secret."
    }
